pe":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSegno","abstract":[{"text":"The segno type is the visual indicator of a segno sign. The exact glyph can be specified with the smufl","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute. A sound element is also needed to guide playback applications reliably.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/segno":{"kind":"symbol","title":"segno","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/segno","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"segno"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLSegnoV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSegno"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/segno","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The visual indicator of a segno sign appearing at this barline."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBarline","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inverted).","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLBarline","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarlin